From 5c61e64c99d523f83907e6e02f3dc2ecb7fcf6d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 01:08:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Wire correlation-based proxy detection into C2 rollup as
 dimension 5

The correlation-based proxy detector (check_correlation_based_proxy_detection,
built July 24) was deliberately left unwired to the C2 rollup last session to
avoid silently changing rollup behavior for existing callers -- it sat in
regulatory_checks.py but CFPBRegBLens.c2_rollup() didn't know about it. Per
request, wired it in today.

New constant DIMENSION_CORRELATION_PROXY_SIGNAL added to regulatory_checks.py.
CFPBRegBLens.c2_rollup() now accepts optional correlation_proxy_findings
parameter (same interface pattern as statistical_outcome_equity_findings --
pass [] for "evaluated and clean", [] for "evaluated with findings", None for
"not yet evaluated" which forces INDETERMINATE). When passed, the correlation
detection dimension is included in the rollup's AND logic.

Updated cfpb_reg_b.py module docstring to document this as dimension 5
(cohort-level like dimension 4), its narrow scope (numeric/boolean only,
string/categorical intentionally unhandled), and how it mitigates the
declared-name screens' vulnerability to variable renaming. Updated disclosed
limitations to note the correlation check as a mitigation.

Tests: 4 new c2_rollup-specific tests (empty correlation findings -> PASS,
flagged correlation findings -> FLAG, None stays INDETERMINATE, proxy screen
and correlation screen can flag together). Fixed 2 existing
test_c2_statistical_outcome_equity.py tests and 2 existing
test_regulatory_cassettes.py tests that were checking dimension counts -- all
now expect both DIMENSION_CORRELATION_PROXY_SIGNAL and
DIMENSION_STATISTICAL_OUTCOME_EQUITY in not_evaluated_dimensions when not
explicitly passed.

Full suite: 456 passed, 6 skipped (452 baseline + 4 new c2_rollup tests),
run twice back-to-back with zero DB reset. ruff (pinned 0.15.22) and
bandit -ll both clean.

This closes out the only remaining open decision from July 24's bundle
delivery: whether to wire the finding-2 correlation mitigation into the
rollup. Now wired and shipped on main.
